index 0000000..4e53cfb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/SOLUTION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+# Solution
+
+Two bugs in `lrucache/cache.py`:
+
+1. **`get` did not count as a "use".** On a hit it returned the value without
+   calling `move_to_end`, so the entry kept its original insertion position in
+   the `OrderedDict`. A key that had just been read was still treated as the
+   least recently used and got evicted by the next `put`. Fixed by moving the
+   key to the end before returning.
+
+2. **`put` evicted on updates to existing keys.** The capacity check was
+   `len(self._data) >= self.capacity` with no test for key membership, so
+   overwriting an already-present key at full capacity popped the oldest entry
+   even though the dict size wasn't going to grow. Fixed by only evicting when
+   the key is new.
